            "creation_time": "2026-08-21T00:15:36Z",
            "text": "Created attachment 3796\nCandidate patch.\n\n## Summary\n\n`do_isna()` and the `coerceTo*()` functions read their argument through the\nelement-at-a-time accessors:\n\n```\n    case REALSXP:\n\tfor (i = 0; i < n; i++)\n\t    pa[i] = ISNAN(REAL_ELT(x, i));\n\tbreak;\n```\n\n`REAL_ELT()` inlines to `ALTREP(x) ? ALTREAL_ELT(x, i) : REAL0(x)[i]`. For an\nALTREP argument that is a virtual dispatch per element. For *any* argument it\nis a per-element branch on the object header which the compiler cannot hoist\npast the writes to `pa`, so the loop does not vectorise.\n\n`anyNA()` -- thirty lines further down the same file -- does not have this\nproblem, because it reads by region:\n\n```\n\tITERATE_BY_REGION(x, xD, i, nbatch, double, REAL, {\n\t\tfor (int k = 0; k < nbatch; k++)\n\t\t    if (ISNAN(xD[k]))\n\t\t\treturn true;\n\t    });\n```\n\nThe reason for the difference looks accidental: `#include <R_ext/Itermacros.h>`\nsits at `coerce.c:2435`, immediately above `anyNA()` and *below* `do_isna()`,\nso `ITERATE_BY_REGION` was simply not in scope where `is.na()` is written.\n\nThe same shape appears in fourteen loops across `coerceToLogical()`,\n`coerceToInteger()`, `coerceToReal()` and `coerceToComplex()`.\n\n## Reproducer\n\n```\nn <- 1e7\ntim <- function(e) {\n    ex <- substitute(e); pf <- parent.frame(); eval(ex, pf)\n    round(1000 * min(replicate(3,\n        system.time(for (.i in 1:20) eval(ex, pf))[[\"elapsed\"]])) / 20, 1)\n}\nmat <- function(x) x[seq_along(x)]          # force materialization\n\ni_alt <- seq_len(n);        i_mat <- mat(i_alt)\nd_alt <- as.numeric(i_alt); d_mat <- mat(d_alt)\nlgl   <- rep_len(c(TRUE, FALSE, NA), n)\n\nc(is.na_altrep_int = tim(is.na(i_alt)), is.na_int  = tim(is.na(i_mat)),\n  is.na_altrep_dbl = tim(is.na(d_alt)), is.na_dbl  = tim(is.na(d_mat)),\n  as.numeric_int   = tim(as.numeric(i_mat)),\n  as.logical_int   = tim(as.logical(i_mat)),\n  anyNA_int        = tim(anyNA(i_mat)),   # reads by region already\n  baseline_d_plus0 = tim(d_mat + 0))\n```\n\nTimes in ms for one call on 10^7 elements. Both columns are the same trunk\nr90424 build on the same machine (macOS 15 / arm64, clang), with and without\nthe patch, so they differ only by the change. Released R 4.6.1 gives the same\nleft-hand column to within run-to-run noise.\n\n| | r90424 | + patch |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `is.na(seq_len(n))` (ALTREP) | 12.6 | **1.1** |\n| `is.na(<integer>)` | 2.9 | **0.8** |\n| `is.na(as.numeric(1:n))` (ALTREP) | 12.4 | **2.0** |\n| `is.na(<double>)` | 2.9 | **1.3** |\n| `is.na(<logical>)` | 2.9 | **0.8** |\n| `is.na(<complex>)` | 2.9 | 2.7 |\n| `as.numeric(<integer>)` | 4.4 | **1.4** |\n| `as.logical(<integer>)` | 3.9 | **0.9** |\n| `as.numeric(<logical>)` | 4.4 | **1.6** |\n| `as.logical(<double>)` | 3.3 | **1.6** |\n| `as.numeric(<raw>)` | 4.2 | **2.7** |\n| `as.complex(<double>)` | 3.4 | **2.3** |\n| `as.integer(<double>)` | 6.0 | **4.0** |\n| `as.numeric(<complex>)` | 5.0 | 5.0 |\n| *`anyNA(<integer>)`, for contrast* | *2.4* | *2.4* |\n| *`d + 0`, for scale* | *1.4* | *1.5* |\n\nThe materialized cases improve as well, so this is not only about ALTREP.\nThe two that do not move are already memory-bound at 16 bytes an element;\n`as.integer(<double>)` gains least because `IntegerFromReal()`'s range checks\ndominate. Nothing measured got slower.\n\n## Patch\n\nTwo parts.\n\n`is.na()`: move the `Itermacros.h` include to the top of the file and switch\nthe four atomic branches of `do_isna()` to `ITERATE_BY_REGION`, exactly as\n`anyNA()` already does.\n\nThe coercions: the fourteen loops have one shape -- run an element converter\nover the source -- so they go through a single `COERCE_BY_REGION` macro\nrather than fourteen copies of the same iteration (net -56 lines).\n`coerceToString()` is left alone because there is no `STRING_GET_REGION`, and\n`coerceToRaw()` because it does its range handling inline rather than calling\na converter, so it does not fit the macro.\n\nNo behaviour changes.\n\n\n## Related, not in this patch\n\n`ISNA()` costs about 6x what the same test costs inlined, because `R_IsNA()`\nis an exported out-of-line function that package code cannot inline through.\nOver 10^7 doubles: `ISNA()` 9.1 ms, the identical payload test inlined 1.5 ms,\n`ISNAN()` 1.1 ms (it inlines to `isnan()`). Giving `ISNA` an inline definition\nin the header, while keeping the function exported for ABI, would close that.",
